.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt QUARK_QUEUE_FILE_ACCESS_NAME_ADD 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm quark_queue_file_access_name_add
.Nd register a file access name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In quark.h
.Ft int
.Fn quark_queue_file_access_name_add "struct quark_queue *qq" "const char *name" "int roles"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Registers
.Fa name ,
a single path component without slashes and shorter than
.Dv QUARK_FILE_ACCESS_NAME_MAX ,
as a name of interest on a queue opened with
.Dv QQ_FILE_ACCESS .
.Fa roles
is a bitmask of
.Dv QUARK_FILE_ACCESS_NAME_LEAF ,
which reports opens of a file called
.Fa name ,
and
.Dv QUARK_FILE_ACCESS_NAME_PARENT ,
which reports opens of any file whose directory, or one of the two directories
above it, is called
.Fa name .
Registering an existing name adds to its roles.
At most
.Dv QUARK_FILE_ACCESS_NAMES_MAX
distinct names can be registered at once; one more fails with
.Er E2BIG .
The names match the leaf and up to three source directories.
A user with a list of full paths registers the leaf of each and
filters the resolved path in the resulting
.Vt quark_file_access
itself.
The components are those of the file on its filesystem, not of the mount it
was reached through: a file under a bind mount is matched against the
directories it has on the underlying filesystem, and the walk stops at the root
of that filesystem.
A mount-point parent name does not match if it exists only in the mount path.
A file bind mount can also have a different visible leaf name.
A component longer than
.Dv QUARK_FILE_ACCESS_NAME_MAX
- 1 bytes matches a registered name equal to its first
.Dv QUARK_FILE_ACCESS_NAME_MAX
- 1 bytes.
The
.Em ruleset
of
.Vt quark_queue_attr
applies to file access events through their process, as to any other event:
a rule on process fields, or
.Dq drop on any ,
drops them.
A
.Em file.path
rule never matches a file access event; the names are the only filter on the
file itself.
.Pp
Opens by all threads of the process that called
.Fn quark_queue_open
are not reported.
A forked child is reported, even if it inherits the queue.
The exclusion ends when the original process exits; a later process with
the same PID is reported.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero on success, -1 on error with
.Va errno
set.
An error leaves the queue usable.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EINVAL
The name is NULL, empty, contains a slash, or has 64 or more bytes;
the roles are zero or contain unknown bits; or the queue does not have
.Dv QQ_FILE_ACCESS
with the eBPF backend.
.It Er E2BIG
The map already has
.Dv QUARK_FILE_ACCESS_NAMES_MAX
distinct names and the new name is not present.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr quark_queue_get_event 3 ,
.Xr quark_queue_open 3 ,
.Xr quark 7
